  "summary_en": "Japan's Road Act Enforcement Regulations (1952, as amended 2026-04-01): ministerial ordinance on road administration, occupancy permits, road ledgers and maintenance. It includes narrow autonomous-driving provisions: performance standards for automated-operation assistance facilities on roads (Art. 4-8-2, 4-8-3) and designation of associations promoting self-driving public transport.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Art. 4-8-2 sets performance standards for roadside automated-operation assistance facilities (sensor-detectable magnetic/radio signals, position and road-condition information) per MLIT standards.",
   "Art. 4-8-3 requires public notice of installation of such facilities.",
   "Art. 4-4-11 lets road administrators designate associations promoting self-driving technology for public transport and logistics.",
   "The rest covers road designation notices, road ledgers, occupancy permits and maintenance inspections."
  ],
